{
  "_comment": [
    "Example `<workdir>/crustify/campaigns/<campaign-id>/schedule.json`.",
    "The campaign's total execution order, emitted once before the first",
    "agent starts. It nests link unit, subsystem, wave -- the same shape as",
    "subsystems.json and as the campaign directory -- and the total order is",
    "that nesting read depth-first. The batches within one wave run in",
    "parallel. A batch entry is exactly the object `crustify translate`",
    "accepts, so writing it out to batch-<index>.json is a copy.",
    "Every index also addresses the filesystem, so no path is recorded.",
    "libbase precedes libwidget because libwidget depends on it: a subsystem's",
    "dependencies in another link unit must belong to an earlier link unit.",
    "Raw-lifetime discovery runs first and has no subsystem of its own."
  ],
